# =============================================================================
# 2. PROVENANCE TREE ROOT  (rollup digest over the whole `provenance/` tree)
# =============================================================================
#
# Command semantics — run from the repo root:
#
#   find provenance -type f -print0 | sort -z | xargs -0 sha256sum | sha256sum
#
# Semantics, precisely:
#   - `find provenance -type f`  — regular files only; directories and symlinks
#     are NOT hashed, so an empty directory does not affect the root digest.
#   - `-print0` / `sort -z` / `xargs -0` — NUL-delimited throughout, so the
#     ordering is a byte-wise sort of the NUL-terminated relative pathnames and
#     is independent of `find` traversal order and of locale-sensitive
#     whitespace/filename handling.
#   - inner `sha256sum` — emits one "<digest>  <relative path>" line per file,
#     in the sorted order above.
#   - outer `sha256sum` — hashes that entire concatenated listing read from
#     stdin. The root digest therefore covers BOTH file contents AND file
#     paths: a pure rename with identical content changes the root.
#   - Output path field is `-` because the outer hash reads stdin.
#
# Any change to content, path, addition, or deletion under provenance/ changes
# this single value.

provenance_tree_files: 70
5e1e5a9867d31d71d8f17cf3ac16a775bbbb4ecd59f7295ce9a31e82ac74f849  -


